DISTRIBUTION SHAPE: ADAPTER-ONLY PUBLIC DEMO

Operator decision, 2026-09-30. Veritas is published as an adapter-only
demonstration. It binds at runtime to operator-provided upstream copies and
reproduces none of them.

Veritas redistributes NONE of the following:

  * state_registry
  * predicate_semantics.py
  * writeback_validator.py
  * outcome_taxonomy.py
  * capability_inventory.py
  * the G1 concept corpus
  * any other internal payload

Self-contained bundling is PROHIBITED until upstream licensing is
explicitly settled by the operator.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

UPSTREAM RIGHTS ARE NOT CONVEYED

This license conveys rights to Veritas' own code only. It grants no rights in
the upstream capabilities named above, and a recipient of this repository
acquires no right to use, copy, or redistribute them by virtue of receiving it.

Upstream ownership and licensing are UNRESOLVED. What was established:

  * state_registry has 17 commits under a single identity (UrukuTelal) and a
    remote at github.com/UrukuTelal/state_registry, but NO LICENSE has ever
    existed in any commit.
  * The four G1 modules are unversioned (C:\G1 is not a git repository),
    unlicensed, and unattributed.
  * All five are stdlib-only, with no vendored subtree and no copyleft
    dependency, so no third-party terms flow through.

Because none of them is redistributed here, publication requires no grant from
anyone. But absent a license they are all-rights-reserved by default, so
Veritas has no durable right to depend on them -- it simply copies nothing out.

No license was added to any upstream project as part of this decision, and none
should be inferred from this repository's presence.

See docs/LICENSING.md for the full analysis and the remaining open question.

